meta {
	name: 10_AdosSubunitInheritance
	seq: 10
}

docs {
	Scenario: The daily leader of an ADOS main unit inherits access to its ADOS subunit

		Given an ADOS (administrativ enhet - offentlig sektor) main unit that has an ADOS subunit
		And a person with the daily leader (DAGL) key role on the ADOS main unit
		When the daily leader lists authorized parties with subunits included
		Then the ADOS main unit is returned
		And the ADOS subunit is nested under the ADOS main unit

	This mirrors the existing BEDR/AAFY subunit inheritance. It verifies the read-side effect
	of the AccessManagement.Subunit.AdosInheritance feature flag: once the ADOS subunit's
	ParentId points to the ADOS main unit, a key role on the main unit carries down to the
	subunit just like for ordinary business subunits.

	Personas come from `testdata/<env>.js` under the `adosMainUnit` key. The ADOS unit and its
	subunit are part of the seeded environment data (a valid ADOS unit that exists in AT22 and
	TT02), so the step reads them rather than creating them.
}
